Z||000000||87GT||10-17-1999||11:09 PM||||I am going to get all new tires on my 87GT sometime in the next few weeks.  My rear tires are pretty worn but the front tires are ok, but I want to change them all to keep them uniform.  Anyways,  I looked into Goodyear tires(Im a fan) and did a online selector at their site and it recommended the Eagle Aquasteel EMT.  I was just wondering if anybody has these particular tires?  If so let me know what you think.  If there are any other stellar tires I should consider, let me know.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shiner||10-18-1999||02:20 AM||||I am going to be in the market for tires soon also.  It seems like if you can get the right size, Firehawk SZ50's would be a great deal.  I belive they are under 100$ a tire, and are z rated.  Check them out at tirerack.com.  They got terrific ratings.  It's kind of hard to get "ultra high performance" rubbber, as tirerack.com calls it, for our stock GT rims. 225/55/15 are identical for speedo purposes to 215/60/15. That gives you a little to work with.  I wouldn't mind if the speedo was 1%-4% off.  Anybody?||||reg||5
Z||000002||lowCG||10-18-1999||09:22 PM||||Have to agree alot with Shiner,I've got the SZ50s on my car;nice tires.I have 225/50 16 on back,and 205/55 16 in front.<BR>Goodyear used to be a good value,but that was a long time ago,Bridgestone/Firestone has so many different,up-to-date designs to choose from,at reasonable prices too.<BR>For once,one of my cars has an accurate speedo.||||reg||1
